// RFC 0038: `print`/`println` are VARIADIC. Every argument after the FIRST used to be
// silently DROPPED (x86_selector.ax read only extras[arg_start+1], retargeted the call to
// a 1-parameter runtime shim and never adjusted arg_count), so `println("val: ", s)`
// printed `val: ` and stopped -- accept-then-miscompile, BUG#53 class.
//
// The MIXED-TYPE call is load-bearing: it fails if anyone "fixes" this by applying the
// FIRST argument's type to every argument. `n=` is a str, `15` an i64, ` b=` a str and
// `true` a bool, all in ONE call.
//
// The non-ASCII segment pins UTF-8 literals end to end: the compiler must carry the raw
// bytes of `Kết quả` from the lexer through the string pool into .rdata untouched. (Any
// mojibake seen at a terminal is the CONSOLE CODEPAGE, not the compiler -- verify with
// `./t_printvariadic.exe | xxd`.)
//
// Kept to ONE output line on purpose: the regression harness captures stdout with command
// substitution, which strips only TRAILING newlines.
fn main() -> i32:
    print("A", "B", "C")
    print("/")
    print("n=", 15, " b=", true)
    print(" f=", 2.5)
    print(" Kết quả: ", 42)
    println(" end")
    return 42
